<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Colombian president to meet S.Africa's Mandela.</title>
<headline>Colombian president to meet S.Africa's Mandela.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombian president Ernesto Samper Pizano is to pay a two-day visit to South Africa starting on May 2, the Department of Foreign affairs said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Colombia is currently the chair of the Non-Aligned Movement group of developing countries and Samper will be talking to President Nelson Mandela on those issues. South Africa is to be the next chair.</p>
</text>
